    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `format_for_display` in `app/report.py`, and all 4 tests pass (the 2 that were already there and 2 new ones).\n\nIt formats each cell with `DataFrame.map`, which returns a new table with the same index and columns and leaves the input unchanged:\n- **Missing** \u2192 `\"\"`\n- **Zero** \u2192 `\"-\"`\n- **Negative** \u2192 `\"(634.20)\"`\n- **Positive** \u2192 `\"12,500.00\"`\n\n**One rule you didn't specify:** amounts are rounded to 2 decimals before the zero check. So a leftover like `-0.001` from summing floats shows as `\"-\"` rather than `\"(0.00)\"`. If you'd rather show those as `(0.00)`, it's a one-line change.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/test_report.py`. They check every rule on a hand-built table, confirm the input is unchanged, and run the function on the real `monthly_pnl` output from the test ledger.\n\nI couldn't check the pandas docs because Context7 was out of quota. I used `DataFrame.map` because `applymap` was removed in pandas 3, and the passing tests confirm it works on the pinned pandas 3.0.6."
  },
